  "content": {
    "id": "p38-q53-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Find the equation of the exponential function $y=k\\times a^{\\pm x}+b$, where $a>0$, that passes through the following points.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p38-q53-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$(0,-3),\\ (2,0),\\ (3,4)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p38-q53-a-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "y=2^x-4",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p38-q53-a-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Substitute the three points and subtract equations to obtain base ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "2",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ", then find ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "k=1",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " and ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "b=-4",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "Write $y=kc^x+b$, where $c>0$ and $c\\ne1$; either sign in the given exponent can be absorbed into the base. Substituting the points gives\n$$\\begin{align*}k+b&=-3\\\\kc^2+b&=0\\\\kc^3+b&=4.\\end{align*}$$\nSubtracting equations gives\n$$\\begin{align*}k(c^2-1)&=3\\\\k(c^3-c^2)&=4.\\end{align*}$$\nDivide these equations and cancel $c-1$:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{c^3-c^2}{c^2-1}&=\\frac43\\\\\\frac{c^2}{c+1}&=\\frac43\\\\3c^2&=4(c+1)\\\\3c^2-4c-4&=0\\\\(3c+2)(c-2)&=0\\\\c&=2.\\end{align*}$$\nThe other root is negative and cannot be an exponential base.\n$$\\begin{align*}k&=\\frac{3}{2^2-1}\\\\k&=1\\\\b&=-3-1\\\\b&=-4\\\\y&=2^x-4.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 180
      },
      {
        "id": "p38-q53-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$(1,0),\\ (2,-4),\\ (3,-12)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
