                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "y=4-2\\times2^x",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p38-q53-b-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The ratio of successive changes gives base ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "2",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "; substitution gives ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "k=-2",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " and ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "b=4",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "Write $y=kc^x+b$, where $c>0$ and $c\\ne1$. Substituting the points gives\n$$\\begin{align*}kc+b&=0\\\\kc^2+b&=-4\\\\kc^3+b&=-12.\\end{align*}$$\nSubtract successive equations:\n$$\\begin{align*}kc(c-1)&=-4\\\\kc^2(c-1)&=-8.\\end{align*}$$\nTheir ratio gives\n$$\\begin{align*}c&=\\frac{-8}{-4}\\\\c&=2\\\\k&=\\frac{-4}{2(2-1)}\\\\k&=-2\\\\b&=-kc\\\\b&=4\\\\y&=4-2\\times2^x.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 134
      },
      {
        "id": "p38-q53-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$(-2,18),\\ (-1,6),\\ (0.5,2.5)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p38-q53-c-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
