                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "y=2+4^{-x}",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p38-q53-c-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Use ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "y=kc^x+b",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " and ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "t=\\sqrt c",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ". Subtract the point equations to find ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "c=\\frac14,\\ k=1,\\ b=2",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "Write $y=kc^x+b$, where $c>0$ and $c\\ne1$, and let $t=\\sqrt c$. Then $t>0$ and $t\\ne1$. Substituting the points gives\n$$\\begin{align*}kt^{-4}+b&=18\\\\kt^{-2}+b&=6\\\\kt+b&=\\frac52.\\end{align*}$$\nSubtract successive equations:\n$$\\begin{align*}k(t^{-4}-t^{-2})&=12\\\\k(t^{-2}-t)&=\\frac72.\\end{align*}$$\nDivide and simplify using index laws:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{24}{7}&=\\frac{t^{-4}-t^{-2}}{t^{-2}-t}\\\\\\frac{24}{7}&=\\frac{1+t}{t^2(1+t+t^2)}.\\end{align*}$$\nHence\n$$\\begin{align*}24t^2(1+t+t^2)&=7(1+t)\\\\24t^4+24t^3+24t^2-7t-7&=0\\\\(2t-1)(12t^3+18t^2+21t+7)&=0.\\end{align*}$$\nThe cubic factor is positive for $t>0$, so\n$$\\begin{align*}t&=\\frac12\\\\c&=\\frac14\\\\k&=\\frac{12}{16-4}\\\\k&=1\\\\b&=6-4\\\\b&=2\\\\y&=2+4^{-x}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
